From 3eec725fd96717610558d611791dedb3ecafa35a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 06:12:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] transport: af-mctp: Fix TID lookup with MCTP_NET_ANY

The pldm_transport_af_mctp_map_tid() API stores TID mappings with
tid_map[tid].net = MCTP_NET_ANY, but pldm_transport_af_mctp_get_tid()
requires an exact network match (tid_map[i].net == network). When MCTP
messages arrive with non-zero network IDs, the lookup fails, causing
pldmd to crash with "free(): invalid pointer" errors.

Fix this by allowing MCTP_NET_ANY in stored mappings to match any
incoming network ID, with exact network matches taking precedence over
MCTP_NET_ANY. This ensures that callers using both map_tid() and
map_tid_fqe() get correct behavior: specific network mappings are
preferred, and MCTP_NET_ANY entries serve only as a fallback.

Add af-mctp test infrastructure in dedicated af-mctp-test.c and
af-mctp-internal.h, keeping test utilities separate from the core
implementation. tests/transport/af-mctp.cpp verifies MCTP_NET_ANY
matches any network, that specific network IDs are correctly
distinguished, and that exact matches take precedence when both mapping
APIs are used together.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Fixes: 6b8f2646bc2a ("transport: af-mctp: Qualify MCTP TID mapping with target network")
Change-Id: Iaf9a0e09681dbfd202af747688b160dba1558692
Signed-off-by: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
---
